WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.070
Which piece of your work has the most roles?

00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:05.810
For example, a release or a launch brief.

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:14.730
Now, in this adventure, you turn it into a multi-agent workflow, for code or documents: several AI agents, each with one job.

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:18.590
And a lead agent hands out the work, several parts at once,

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:21.180
then decides what's next as results arrive.

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:24.420
So the plan changes with what each agent finds,

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:26.630
and a reviewer can send work back.

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:33.090
Then you approve once, on the monday board, Slack channel or folder where the work already lives.

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:39.490
It's like a newsroom: an editor assigns several reporters, a fact-checker sends a draft back,

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:42.110
and you, the editor-in-chief, sign off.

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:47.070
But often, one agent is enough, so each extra one must earn its place.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:50.750
So in this adventure, you build your multi-agent workflow,

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:54.070
until a second real run needs only small edits.
